[h1]Dungeon Delve - Battle Royale 0.19.0[/h1]
A private 2-4 player PvPvE race across three dungeon floors. Loot, choose your build, fight rivals, and claim a final-floor exit. Death brings monster returns, then rats -- not the end of your match!

[b]REQUIRES the separately downloaded vending_machine framework runtime. Subscribing alone will NOT enable this game mode.[/b]
[url=[FRAMEWORK_WORKSHOP_URL]]Framework, required runtime download and installation instructions[/url]
Windows x64 / tested Steam Barony 5.0.2. Every player needs both 0.19.0 subscriptions and the matching runtime (protocol 30 / API 1).

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Mines, Jungle and Crystal Caves: three native-generated 90x90 floors, six minutes each, harder enemies deeper down, 1.75x XP.
[*]One single-use hatch and three portals per floor. First portal at 1:00 remaining; two more at timeout. Final-floor exits open no earlier than the last minute: first accepted claim wins.
[*]Escalating boulder storms at timeout, or the last minute on the final floor.
[*]Random floor-scaled rarity loot, equipment/spellbook affixes, readable rarity slots and world-drop smoke.
[*]26 classes with selectable passives/abilities. Q/E activate abilities by default. Genuine per-player DLC ownership remains required for DLC characters.
[*]Adventurer levels/stats/proficiencies survive death within the match. New matches start fresh; no persistent loot banks.
[*]17 monster forms, then fragile rats with normal uncapped damage and 45-second repeat-death respawns. Eat 10 cheese pieces in one rat life to become Algernon.
[*]No minimum skill/INT requirement to learn spells; rarer spellbooks keep progression in check.
[*]Improved monster picker, furnished Last Hearth lobby, three recorded floor introductions with subtitles.
[/list]

[h2]How to play[/h2]
Subscribe to this item and its required framework. Download/extract the runtime linked on the framework page. Read its README, then launch Play-Dungeon-Delve.cmd, not retail Barony. Host/join a fresh private Direct IP lobby; everyone joins before starting and the host remains until results. Do not mix raid/normal clients, other native frameworks, campaign imports or Join In Progress.

[h2]Experimental release[/h2]
Windows x64 only; no Steam matchmaking/invites or hardened public servers. WAN and human balance testing remain limited. Retail executable/saves/config stay separate; every launch uses a fresh isolated session. See the included README for complete current rules, logs, updates and uninstall. Unofficial project, not an official Barony update.
